# A dm-verity device is ready as soon as device-mapper set it up, even when
# its content cannot be read. systemd's 99-systemd.rules marks encrypted
# devices (DM_UUID CRYPT-*) without a recognised file system not ready,
# "since we are probably still calling mke2fs" – which matches verity
# (CRYPT-VERITY-*) too, although a verity device is read-only and fixed by
# its root hash: it never gets a file system later. With a modified /usr,
# blkid's probe fails (I/O error), the device never became ready, and the
# initrd waited the full 90 s device timeout before the emergency gate. Now
# the mount fails at once with the real error. Sorted after 99-systemd.rules.
# Upstream report: ~/upstream.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ACTION!="remove", ENV{DM_UUID}=="CRYPT-VERITY-*", ENV{DM_NAME}=="?*", \
  ENV{DM_UDEV_DISABLE_OTHER_RULES_FLAG}!="1", ENV{ID_PART_TABLE_TYPE}=="", ENV{ID_FS_USAGE}=="", \
  ENV{SYSTEMD_READY}="1"
